    "updated_at": "2022-05-02T15:31:39Z",
    "body": "These also seem suspect:\r\n\r\n> If one of the controls is not [being rendered](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#being-rendered) (e.g. it has the [hidden](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#attr-hidden) attribute set) then user agents may report a script error.\r\n\r\n> Neither the element nor any of its ancestors has a [hidden](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#attr-hidden) attribute specified.\r\n\r\n> The presence of the [hidden](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#attr-hidden) attribute normally means the element is not [being rendered](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#being-rendered), though this might be overridden by the style sheets.\r\n\r\nI wonder if there are more such instances that assume it's a boolean.",
